{
  "description": "Lithuanian labels for the record keys the dashboard would otherwise de-slug. `labelFor` in dashboard/index.html resolves a key against SECTION_LABELS, the concept map's `label-lt`, the concept map's path segments, then this file, then `deslug` -- which lower-cases an ASCII-folded slug and cannot restore a diacritic. Measured over all 113,073 records (issue #149): 480 distinct keys reach a label and 398 of them fell through to deslug, 125 of those provably mis-spelled -- 'Pavarde', 'Darboviete', 'Numeris sarase', 'Seimos nariu skaicius' -- and 47 printed in English ('Row number' on 4,020,284 cells). Each entry carries the proof of its label: `printed` (the string VRK prints, so that scraper.shared.files.slugify(label) == key, which is how the parser made the key -- the one normalization applied is a capital first letter); `header` (the column heading VRK prints above the value, quoted from the archived pages under samples/); `restored` (the key's own words with their diacritics and case restored, so folding the label reproduces the key word for word); `structural` (a key the parsers invented and no VRK page labels, translated here). tests/test_dashboard_field_labels.py holds each of those four claims, and that every key still occurs in the corpus.",
  "verified": "2026-09-10 against all 113,073 records: every key below occurs in the normalized layer (or the root kandidatavimas block) of at least one record, every `printed` label is a string the corpus's own rawData holds, and no entry duplicates what deslug already produces.",
